{"id": "tea:ocean-of-reasoning:ch.24", "source": "src:ocean-of-reasoning", "location": {"ref": "ch.24"}, "paraphrase": "Commenting on 'for whom emptiness is possible, everything is possible' (MMK 24.14), Tsongkhapa argues that the opponent who charges emptiness with destroying the four truths has it backwards: only because things are empty of inherent existence can arising, ceasing, the truths and the path be posited.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:tsongkhapa"], "commentary_on": "tea:mulamadhyamakakarika:24.14", "disputes": ["dsp:madhyamaka-nihilism-charge"], "notes": "Chapter-level ref.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
